= The Judiciary

Courts shape every policy fight. Federal judges serve for life, so choices made today last for decades.

- @appoint_judges: Prioritize judicial appointments
- @bipartisan_picks: Seek consensus nominees
- @court_reform_push: Push structural court reform
- @easy_discard

@appoint_judges
subtitle: needs Senate control
unavailable-subtitle: Needs a Democratic Senate.
choose-if: dem_senate = 1
on-arrival: courts_independence += 3; court_lean -= 0.4; progressive_dissent -= 2; month_actions += 1

We move nominees through the Senate and fill vacancies.

@bipartisan_picks
on-arrival: courts_independence += 4; gopmod_relation += 4; progressive_dissent += 3; institutions += 1; month_actions += 1

We pick respected jurists acceptable across the spectrum.

@court_reform_push
subtitle: needs Congress
unavailable-subtitle: Needs both chambers.
choose-if: dem_senate = 1 and dem_house = 1
on-arrival: court_reform += 1; court_lean -= 1; progressive_dissent -= 5; moderate_dissent += 5; institutions -= 1; polarization += 2; trump_urgency += 0.3; month_actions += 1

Term limits and expansion spark a firestorm.
